  "summary": "Reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges per RBC-TOC-02, with a progress note for each patient (plus an addendum note where new items changed a decision).\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005): furosemide changed to 40 mg BID per signed addendum (mr-t0001). KCl stopped. Omeprazole kept (pantoprazole was a formulary substitution). Lisinopril first stayed held (K 5.4 on 10/21); 10/23 BMP then came in (K 4.7, SCr 1.21), so it was resumed. FLAG: task-t0003 is superseded but I couldn't close it. An unsigned draft addendum proposes furosemide 60 mg BID; not acted on; message comm-t0022.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004): carvedilol briefly went to 12.5 mg BID; a signed addendum then reversed it, so it's back to 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0016); no net change. FLAGS: low atorvastatin fills (~24% coverage), no change made, comm-t0006. Outside glipizide (Dr. Desai) not addressed by the discharge summary and on top of insulin 70/30, comm-t0007.\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044): lisinopril resumed on 10/22 labs, then held again when K 5.5 came in on 10/23. FLAG: task-t0018, due 10/27.\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069): lisinopril resumed (post-discharge SCr 1.12, K 4.4); other meds unchanged.\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067): metformin stays held; the only creatinine was drawn in hospital, before discharge. Task task-t0013 due 10/24 for the post-discharge BMP.\n\nThe four new inbox items for these patients were reviewed and closed.",
